SUMMARY:Comics Crashcourse: Grades 6-9 at PCA&D
DESCRIPTION:Comic books bring visually striking illustration to life with creative writing and pages upon pages of panels that take readers through vast worlds and detailed stories. The art of making comics is just as intricate and exciting. Have you ever wished you could bring your stories to life through the art of comics? If you enjoy creative writing\, character building\, and storyboarding this class is the perfect place for you to combine those skills and learn something new! Join us as we create our own short comics from the ground up and learn the basics of what it takes become your very own indie comic creator. This is a studio based class for students in grades 6-9 with some lecture\, lots of guidance\, and demonstration. Expect to have lots of creative freedom within the bounds of the assignment! \n            \n        \n                \n            \n                \n                \n    Register Now
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/comics-crashcourse-grades-6-9-at-pcad/
LOCATION:Pennsylvania College of Art & Design – Center for Creative Exploration\, 204 North Prince Street\, Lancaster\, Pennsylvania\, 17603\, United States
